WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Do your genes tell a story?

00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:08,500
All 20,000 of them wrapped up in 23 pairs of chromosomes can guide a future and shape a destiny.

00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,500
However, that's only part of your biography.

00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,500
It is what you do with your genes that make the difference.

00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,000
If you know your genes, it's like owning your map.

00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
There are roads to different places.

00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,500
Some roads are highways and others are gravel.

00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,500
Some places are where you want to go.

00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Others are what you want to avoid.

00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,500
The more you understand the map, the better choices you can make to arrive at the destination you desire.

00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:39,500
Dr. Conner's complete genetic report is like a GPS that helps guide you, so you become the driver on the highways of life.

00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,500
You choose the destination and direction.

00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,500
Your road of life will present many choices.

00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,500
Knowing the path less traveled by will make all the difference.

00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,500
Your genes are the words.

00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,500
You write the story.

00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,500
Let Dr. Conner's help you write your autobiography.

00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:04,500
